                  <items count="4">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Turn a wall-thickness field (e.g. from Shell BESO) into a target layer height per vertex.
Mapping 0 = constant bead area: fixed flow and feed, so a lower layer squashes the bead wider. Thick walls get thin layers.
Mapping 1 = linear: thickest wall gets hMin, thinnest gets hMax.
Mapping 2 = constant aspect ratio h = k·t: every bead is squashed the same amount. Needs flow control: use the Flow Factor output of Non-planar Layers.</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">48c7ae7c-8f02-4ace-a141-0be341a06449</item>
